SUMMARY:Do Not Sit: Exhibition by Samuel Elijah Lee and Grace Kaneshiro
DESCRIPTION:The Program in Visual Arts and Department of Art & Archaeolog
 y present a showing of works collaboratively realized by Practice of Art
  major Samuel Elijah Lee ‘27 and Grace Kaneshiro ’27\, a visual arts
  minor. Artists' Statement The works presented in Do Not Sit are a rumin
 ation on the physical\, metaphorical\, and theoretical human and non-hum
 an relationships between objects and bodies. This show is not about chai
 rs. In some ways\, these works are meant to interrogate the contradictio
 ns found in ordinary objects such as the chair\, which on one hand repre
 sent modes of stasis and rest\, but on the ot\nhttps://www.princeton.edu
 /events/2026/do-not-sit-exhibition-samuel-elijah-lee-and-grace-kaneshiro
