SUMMARY:The Black Arts Collective: My Kids Will Call You Auntie
DESCRIPTION:Members of the Princeton University student group The Black A
 rts Collective present an exhibition of new work in a variety of mediums
 .Collective Artist StatementMy Kids Will Call You Auntie amplifies and i
 ntertwines with Priya Vulchi’s “Good Friends”\, a monograph framin
 g friendship as an act of love and resistance—as a powerful political 
 tool. Seventeen members of The Black Arts Collective provoke an intensif
 ication of the value of platonic relationships under a political climate
  determined to force us into isolation. Upcycling the definition of frie
 ndship\, we reimagine a ‘friend’ as a pillar \nhttps://www.princeton
 .edu/events/2026/black-arts-collective-my-kids-will-call-you-auntie-1
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/black-arts-collective-my-kids-w
 ill-call-you-auntie-1
