SUMMARY:Repujado: Light\, Shadow & Story
DESCRIPTION:What happens when light becomes part of the artwork?Explore r
 epujado\, a traditional Mexican metal-embossing technique\, through the 
 interplay of surface\, light\, shadow\, and visual storytelling.In this 
 hands-on workshop\, participants will experiment with line\, texture\, p
 attern\, and depth\, discovering how raised and recessed metal surfaces 
 respond to light. As light moves across the embossed surface\, highlight
 s and shadows reveal new details\, creating a sense of depth\, movement\
 , and transformation.Participants will create an original embossed metal
  piece inspired by an object\, character\, symbol\, \nhttps://www.prince
 ton.edu/events/2026/repujado-light-shadow-story
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/repujado-light-shadow-story
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
