  contrasts. The concert opens with Britten's Four Sea Interludes from Pe
 ter Grimes\, a set of orchestral tableaux that capture the shifting mood
 s of the English coast. The program concludes with Tchaikovsky's Symphon
 y No. 6 in B minor\, "Pathétique\," the composer's final symphonic stat
 ement — a work of sweeping emotional depth\, from turbulent unrest to 
 quiet\, devastating resignation.Conducted by Michael Pratt\, Professor o
 f the Practice\, Director of Program in Music Performance\, and Director
