SUMMARY:Dmitri Tymoczko: ‘5x5’ + Max Vinetz: ‘felt felt felt felt
 ’
DESCRIPTION:Princeton University faculty composer Dmitri Tymoczko’s new
  25-minute work\, ‘5x5’\, written for solo piano and performed by Am
 y Yang\, is a set of five piano pieces that represents the composer’s 
 renewed interest in repetition and in trying to draw on elements of the 
 classical tradition. Graduate student composer Max Vinetz’s new work 
 ‘felt felt felt felt’ is an album-length saxophone quartet commissio
 ned by the Aruna Quartet that draws on the physical construction and sou
 nd-production methods of the saxophone\, the abstraction of pop style me
 lody and song structure\, and an exploration of the qua\nhttps://www.pri
 nceton.edu/events/2026/dmitri-tymoczko-5x5-max-vinetz-felt-felt-felt-fel
 t
